// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  CATACOMB (V147–V149) — the way into a chapel is DOWN. Beside the chapel, in its churchyard, a mausoleum; its stair goes
//  down into the catacombs where the town's faithful are buried — and, deepest of all, its general. A dungeon in the
//  Ocarina manner, the same every time you play: small keys for locked doors, one map and one compass for the whole of it,
//  sarcophagi to shove onto pressure plates, lamps to light before the first gutters out, a floor that gives way, a
//  mini-boss, and at the bottom the general's tomb — his spirit spars with you (it teaches the parry), asks the doctrine he
//  died defending, and gives you his relic, the dungeon's item. Hearthvale's is the SHEPHERD'S STAFF: a crook that catches
//  iron rings across a chasm and swings you over, pulls levers out of reach, and drags a stone ossuary toward you. With it
//  the way back opens: the boss key, the great door, and the stair up into the chapel's nave, where the guardian waits.
//  Cleansed, the catacombs stay open — candlelit, quiet, the brothers tending the tombs again.
//  Rooms you clear stay cleared; every door you open stays open (GAME.S.cata[town]).
//  Layout legend:  # rock · . floor · , open archway · S the stair out (to the churchyard) · v a stair down · u a stair up
//   N the stair up into the nave · L locked door (small key) · G the great door (boss key) · 1-9 iron gates (the floor's rules)
//   C chest · Q the great chest (the boss key) · T sarcophagus · A the general's tomb · B a stone ossuary you push (or pull)
//   P pressure plate · O pillar · l lamp · t tablet · k lectern (the brothers' records) · X chasm · R an iron ring on a post
//   Y lever · K cracked floor (it gives way) · p c b s demons on their posts (pouncer, clawer, brute, spitter) · m the Warden
//  CATACOMB.attach(world, {town, door, td, C, nave(), cleansed()})  ·  levels 'cata<town>:<n>'
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
